    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "TIT",
      "chapter": 2,
      "chapter_usfm": "TIT.2",
      "version_id": 72,
      "version_abbr": "HCSB",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But you must say the things that are consistent with sound teaching."
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Older men are to be level headed, worthy of respect, sensible, and sound in faith, love, and endurance."
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "In the same way, older women are to be reverent in behavior, not slanderers, not addicted to much wine. They are to teach what is good,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "so they may encourage the young women to love their husbands and to love their children,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "to be self-controlled, pure, homemakers, kind, and submissive to their husbands, so that God’s message will not be slandered."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "In the same way, encourage the young men to be self-controlled"
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "in everything. Make yourself an example of good works with integrity and dignity in your teaching."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Your message is to be sound beyond reproach, so that the opponent will be ashamed, having nothing bad to say about us."
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Slaves are to be submissive to their masters in everything, and to be well-pleasing, not talking back"
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "or stealing, but demonstrating utter faithfulness, so that they may adorn the teaching of God our Savior in everything."
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For the grace of God has appeared with salvation for all people,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "instructing us to deny godlessness and worldly lusts and to live in a sensible, righteous, and godly way in the present age,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "while we wait for the blessed hope and appearing of the glory of our great God and Savior, Jesus Christ."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "He gave Himself for us to redeem us from all lawlessness and to cleanse for Himself a people for His own possession, eager to do good works."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Say these things, and encourage and rebuke with all authority. Let no one disregard you."
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 15,
